---
title: Pasta al pomodoro
author: Easy Recipes
servings: 2
time: 25 minutes
cuisine: Italian
category: Pasta
tags: Quick, Vegetarian
description: The everyday Italian classic — a quick tomato sauce with garlic and basil.
---

Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add @coarse salt{1%tbsp}.

Meanwhile, warm @extra virgin olive oil{3%tbsp} in a #large pan{} over low heat. Add @garlic{2%cloves}, lightly crushed, and cook for ~{2%minutes} without letting it brown.

Add @tomato passata{400%ml} and a pinch of @salt{}. Simmer for ~{15%minutes}, stirring now and then.

Cook @spaghetti{200%g} in the boiling water for ~{9%minutes} — one minute less than the package says.

Drain the pasta, keeping a cup of the cooking water. Toss the pasta in the sauce for ~{1%minute}, adding a splash of the water if it looks dry.

Turn off the heat, tear in @fresh basil{6%leaves} and finish with grated @parmesan{30%g}.
